.TH "SKOGAI RUNNER-SEND" 1  "skogai runner-send 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai runner\-send \- send a prompt and files to an agent, print its typed output
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai runner send\fR [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
send a prompt and files to an agent, print its typed output
.br

.br
the prompt comes from \-\-prompt or stdin. files are inlined as
.br
<file path="..."> blocks, so the agent needs no tools to read them.
.br
with \-\-schema stdout is the json object, without it plain text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-prompt\fR=\fIPROMPT\fR
.br
prompt text, read from stdin if omitted
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR=[\fIFILE\fR]...
.br
file to inline
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-schema\fR=\fISCHEMA\fR
.br
schema name or path for the output
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR=\fIMODEL\fR
.br
model, default runner.model
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tools\fR=\fITOOLS\fR
.br
tools the agent may use, none if omitted
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-allow\fR=[\fIALLOW\fR]...
.br
allowed tool patterns, e.g. "Bash(git log *)"
.TP
\fB\-\-plugin\-dir\fR=[\fIDIR\fR]...
.br
plugin to load into the agent
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
.br
print the full result envelope
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
